<%#
  Hook 3 (render_plugin_partials): "date_fields_ext" is rendered at the end
  of the shared date subrecord template (dates/_template.html.erb), after
  the certainty/era/calendar fields -- so it appears inside every date
  subrecord form, across every record type that has dates (resources,
  accessions, archival objects, etc). Locals: :form (the date subrecord's
  own form context, not the parent record's).

  This renders a field row in the same markup shape as certainty/era/
  calendar just above it (label_and_select, via label_with_field in
  aspace_form_helper.rb -- see _basic_information_resource.html.erb for
  more on that shared shape), so it's a genuine-looking new row on the
  Dates form. The input is disabled and labeled as such, though: this hook
  only controls where something is drawn on the page, so even an enabled
  input here wouldn't go anywhere on submit -- ArchivesSpace has no
  "source_note" field on a date subrecord to save it into. Making a field
  like this actually save requires real plugin work beyond the frontend --
  extending the schema, a migration, and usually an indexer change (see the
  `hello_world` plugin for that full pattern).
%>
<div class="form-group w-100 row">
  <label class="control-label text-right col-sm-2" for="plugin_hooks_example_date_source_note">
    plugin_hooks_example: Source Note
  </label>
  <div class="col-sm-9">
    <input
      type="text"
      id="plugin_hooks_example_date_source_note"
      class="form-control"
      disabled
      placeholder="e.g. Date confirmed via donor correspondence, box 4"
    />
    <p class="text-muted small mb-0">
      Disabled -- this field isn't real. Typing here wouldn't save
      anything; that needs real backend plugin work.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
